    assert (a1>0 and a2>0), "Invalid shapes"
----------------------------------------    print("Shape 1 is : ", s1.typ) if a1>a2 else print("Shape 2 is : ", s2.typ)
    # return

def compare_p(s1, s2):
    '''returns area of shape with larger perimeter'''
    a1, a2 = s1.perimeter, s2.perimeter
    print("Shape 1 is : ", s1.typ) if a1>a2 else print("Shape 2 is : ", s2.typ)
    # return


# Test Cases
r1 = Rectangle(3,7)
r2 = Rectangle(4,6)
c1 = Circle(5)
c2 = Circle(7)

compare_a(r1,r2)
compare_a(c1,c2)

compare_p(r1,r2)
compare_p(c1,c2)
```

This is a python code snippet for implementing the strategy for shape comparisons. The program defines a parent class "Shape", and then defines two types of shapes "Rectangle" and "Circle" which are derived from the "Shape" class. Every shape has an area and perimeter which are calculated in their respective constructors. The function compare_a, compare_p function are comparing shapes based on their area and perimeter, respectively.

```bash
Shape 1 is :  Rectangle
Shape 1 is :  Circle
Shape 2 is :  Rectangle
Shape 2 is :  Circle
